The themes the app can wear (pick one in the app's Settings, or with
`amarchy theme <name>`), one folder each:

colors.toml
  The theme's palette, exactly as Omarchy ships it (themes/<name>/colors.toml
  at basecamp/omarchy 3c7027d, 2026-10-22). Omarchy is MIT licensed, copyright
  David Heinemeier Hansson: LICENSE-omarchy. Several palettes are Omarchy's
  takes on color schemes of their own (Catppuccin, Everforest, Flexoki,
  Gruvbox, Kanagawa, Nord, Rosé Pine, Tokyo Night), each MIT licensed by its
  authors.

theme.toml
  amarchy's: the theme's name, the style its wallpaper is drawn in, and what
  Omarchy's hyprland.lua for the theme changes (its border colors, rounded
  corners, how see-through its terminals are).

wallpaper.svg, wallpaper-wide.svg
  amarchy's own, drawn by make.py from the palette, for a phone and for a
  computer's screen. Run it to draw them again. Omarchy's own wallpapers
  aren't here: they come without a word on who made them or under what
  license.
